# .shopifyignore — controls what Shopify CLI syncs to/from the store.
#
# Note: the CLI only ever uploads recognised theme directories (assets, blocks,
# config, layout, locales, sections, snippets, templates). Repo-level files such
# as README.md, .github/, .vscode/, .prettierrc.json and .theme-check.yml are
# never uploaded, so they do not need listing here.

# Editor and OS noise, in case any of it lands inside a theme directory.
.DS_Store
*.map

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# config/settings_data.json — READ BEFORE UNCOMMENTING
#
# This file holds the *values* behind the theme settings (colour schemes,
# typography, spacing) plus every section's content. It is edited both here and
# by anyone using the theme editor in the Shopify admin.
#
# During the build, we WANT it synced: the design system work in
# settings_schema.json is meaningless without its values, and it should be in
# version control.
#
# At launch, once Melt start customising in the admin, `shopify theme push`
# would overwrite their work. At that point, uncomment the line below so pushes
# stop clobbering merchant edits, and pull deliberately with `shopify theme pull
# --only config/settings_data.json` when you want their changes locally.
#
# config/settings_data.json
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
